        "added_semantics": "Each member carries TWO dates and they mean different things. `added` is the index-inclusion mask: the first date this member's price counts toward the basket's equal-weight level, back-projected to seed_date for any roster curated later, and it is what engine/baskets.py and its sibling engines read. `curated_added` is the provenance stamp: the date a curator actually put this name in this basket, never earlier than the basket's own `created`. Read `curated_added` — never `added` — when asking how long a name has been watched, or whether a signal predates its curation.",
        "construction": "Equal-weight baskets, rebalanced monthly.",
        "curated": "2026-08-07",
        "history_note": "Available history comes from the S&P 1500 and baskets-only price caches. Basket levels are BACK-PROJECTED: a basket curated after seed_date is charted with its current roster carried backward over that roster's own price history, so the line shows what today's members did in the past, not what anyone held at the time. 35 of the 49 baskets here are back-projected this way. Membership changes are recorded per basket in `changelog`, and each member carries its true curation date in `curated_added` (see `added_semantics`) — treat the history before a member's `curated_added` as context, never as a track record.",
        "note": "Curated US theme baskets for monitoring rotation. Descriptive only, not a buy list.",
        "seed_date": "2023-05-09",
        "version": "2026-08-07"
      },
      "sha256": "b968e9812f60494bd02bbc0d5ad4b8dc67dcb90a939426728e9db6befba9678a",
