      "sha256": "f5b752334b571f1f3577bef677db4c6752cd134a2b415989f8122eec739aa666",
      "text_preview": "schema: mastermind.market_reference/v1\ngenerated_note: >\n  MOR-1 first inventory (34 entries). Approved editorial copy from the principal's\n  registry draft, unchanged, with owner_ref anchors corrected to REAL id= anchors\n  verified against the live templates (MOR-1 build packet DEVIATIONS table records\n  every adjustment). No live values. No internal names, repo paths, or engine\n  identifiers. owner_ref values are product surfaces only.\n\nentries:\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Orientation indicator set (1-12)\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  - id: market-regime\n    kind: indicator\n    family: regime\n    label_en: Market Regime\n    label_zh: 市场状态\n    aliases_en: [regime call, market posture read, regime badge]\n    aliases_zh: [市场态势, 市场状态判断, 市场状态徽标]\n    short_definition_en: >\n      A plain-word read of the market's current posture — risk-on, mixed, or risk-off — drawn\n      from the dashboard's composite indicators, shown alongside the day's briefing.\n    short_definition_zh: >\n      对市场当前态势的简明判断——风险偏好、混合或避险——来自看板综合指标，与当日简报一并展示。\n    why_it_matters_en: >\n      Gives a fast, one-word orientation before reading any detail, so you know whether the\n      backdrop currently favours or discourages taking risk.\n    why_it_matters_zh: >\n      在查看细节前先给出一个词的方向感，帮助判断当前环境是偏向承担风险还是偏向谨慎。\n    unit_or_basis: Categorical label (risk-on / mixed / risk-off)\n    unit_or_basis_zh: '分类标签（风险偏好／混合／避险）'\n    interpretation_up: >\n      Risk-on — supportive backdrop; trend, breadth, and cross-asset signals broadly line up.\n    interpretation_up_zh: '风险偏好——环境偏支持性；趋势、广度与跨资产信号总体一致。'\n    interpretation_down: >\n      Risk-off — stressed backdrop; tape under pressure and trend pointing lower.\n    interpretation_down_zh: '避险——环境承压；盘面承压，趋势向下。'\n    interpretation_neutral: >\n      Mixed — signals disagree or the regime is in transition; treat with extra caution.\n    interpretation_neutral_zh: '混合——信号不一致或市场状态处于转换期，应格外谨慎。'\n    caveats_en:\n      - A confirmation-style read of current conditions, not a forecast of what happens next.\n      - Can change quickly when underlying signals flip; check the update time before acting.\n    caveats_zh:\n      - 这是对当前状态的确认性判断，不是对未来走势的预测。\n      - 底层信号变化时该判断可能迅速更新，行动前请核对更新时间。\n    owner_ref: aibrief.html\n    public_source_refs: []\n    related_ids: [market-state-score, regime-quadrant, transition-state]\n    authority_ceiling: reference_only\n    status: active\n\n  - id: market-state-score\n    kind: indicator\n    family: regime\n    label_en: Market State Score\n    label_zh: 市场状态分\n    aliases_en: [state dial, 0-100 market score]\n    aliases_zh: [市场状态评分, 状态仪表盘]\n    short_definition_en: >\n      A 0-100 dial summarising current US equity market posture, blending trend, cross-asset\n      risk appetite, volatility, breadth, liquidity, and stress into one composite read.\n    short_definition_zh: '0-100综合仪表盘，反映美股当前市场态势，综合趋势、跨资产风险偏好、波动率、市场广度、流动性与压力六项因子。'\n    why_it_matters_en: >\n      Turns six separate market inputs into one glanceable number so you can track whether\n      conditions are improving or deteriorating day to day.\n    why_it_matters_zh: >\n      将六项市场输入合并为一个直观数字，方便逐日跟踪环境是在改善还是在恶化。\n    unit_or_basis: 0-100 composite score\n    unit_or_basis_zh: '0-100综合评分'\n    interpretation_up: >\n      Higher score — trend, breadth, and cross-asset signals broadly align supportive.\n    interpretation_up_zh: '评分较高——趋势、广度与跨资产信号总体呈支持性一致。'\n    interpretation_down: >\n      Lower score — tape under stress, trend pointing lower, signals aligned negative.\n    interpretation_down_zh: '评分较低——盘面承压，趋势向下，信号呈负面一致。'\n    interpretation_neutral: >\n      Mid-range score — components disagree or the picture is transitional.\n    interpretation_neutral_zh: '评分处于中间区间——各分项不一致，或整体格局处于过渡阶段。'\n    caveats_en:\n      - A blended confirmation measure of current conditions, not a predictive score.\n      - Individual component legs can pull the score in different directions; check the\n        breakdown before drawing conclusions from the headline number alone.\n    caveats_zh:\n      - 这是对当前状态的综合确认性衡量，不是预测性评分。\n      - 各分项因子可能方向不一致，仅看总分容易误判，建议查看分项拆解。\n    owner_ref: macro.html#regime-radar\n    public_source_refs: []\n    related_ids: [market-regime, market-breadth, evidence-liquidity]\n    authority_ceiling: reference_only\n    status: active\n\n  - id: regime-quadrant\n    kind: indicator\n    family: regime\n    label_en: Regime Quadrant\n    label_zh: 宏观象限\n    aliases_en: [growth-inflation quadrant, macro quadrant]\n    aliases_zh: [增长通胀象限, 经济周期象限]\n    short_definition_en: >\n      A four-way classification of the macro backdrop by the direction of growth and inflation:\n      e.g. growth rising with inflation falling, or growth falling with inflation rising.\n    short_definition_zh: '按增长与通胀的方向变化，将宏观环境划分为四种象限：例如增长上行、通胀下行，或增长下行、通胀上行等组合。'\n    why_it_matters_en: >\n      Different quadrants historically favour different sectors and factors, so it helps frame\n      which parts of the market the",
